rota lap 5052, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; read the threshold plus standfast, reds-first, and the three depths of removal. Its reading: a defect is easiest to see against the dark, so read the ledger of what stands over a ceiling before reading anything new.
think Opened the round with fleet_round_open, launched the cold endurance run detached, then read construction/ITINERARY.md whole. My last lap left one reading open -- settlement/README.md at grade 11 against the Door setting's 9 -- and left eleven front doors standing over the 20 percent ceiling unrostered.
think Ranked the eleven by inbound citers rather than by percentage, since Lindy asks which page is read most. recursion-prompts/README.md leads at 24 citers and 7,878 bytes; the two lineage doors at 33 percent carry 6 and 2.
think Read the page and found a truth fault the register reading could never have named. Its Watching a run live section teaches /tmp/claude_lap.jsonl three times -- once inside the runnable code block, twice in prose -- and tools/f/fleet-loop.sh has written session-output/<seat>.jsonl and session-output/<seat>.txt inside the tree since REDS %549 and %620 seated that habit.
think Checked why nothing caught it: shared_pen reads tracked RUNNERS, a .sh or .rish suffix or a shebang, so a README sits outside the only meter in the tree that reads for this shape. Confirmed by running the scan and grepping its site list.
obs Repaired the teaching first and the register second, in that order, because the register sweep would have touched the same paragraphs either way and a correct sentence is cheaper to recast than a wrong one is to preserve.
obs Register fell 23 percent of 26 sentences to 0 of 39 -- the Radiant floor rather than the Door ceiling -- from six recasts and seven sentence splits. Reach fell grade 11 to 8, which closes the reading last lap left open one room over. B/83 to A/94; every path, number and proper noun held.
obs Rostered the page on DOOR and declared its setting, then proved the wall from both sides: restoring the committed bytes makes prose_register read door_over_ceiling=1 and refuse register_drift.
obs Two runner sites still spell the elder path -- tools/l/launch-claude-chapter.rish and a comment in tools/s/stream_render.jq -- and both live under shared_pen at constant_pen_files=40 against a ceiling of 41. Named on the card, untouched: moving a peer's ceiling is their lane, and fire cuts exactly as deep as the truth requires.
obs Shelving the elder account taught its own small lesson -- the copied body carried a link relative to the card's depth, which reads dead one directory down. Repointed by hand and the shelf graded A/94 from B+/89.
